Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.82,0:00:24.15,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.60,0:00:28.61,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,May I carry that one, as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.96,0:00:32.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, please do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.41,0:02:36.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:02:27.41,0:02:36.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.41,0:02:36.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.79,0:02:58.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh, right... The villa...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.53,0:03:07.17,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia, good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.17,0:03:09.32,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,May I come in?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.32,0:03:10.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ilia?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.67,0:03:16.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming every morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.83,0:03:18.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You may come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.96,0:03:20.20,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.18,0:03:27.10,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Did you sleep well last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.55,0:03:33.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, quite well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.93,0:03:40.95,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Have you grown accustomed to this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.95,0:03:44.54,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, and the move has proceeded smoothly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.21,0:03:51.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A lot has happened, but thanks to Miss Anis, \NI'm not seen as a mere curiosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.82,0:03:53.92,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That is wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.35,0:03:59.33,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I hate to say this immediately \Nafter things have settled down,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.87,0:04:03.75,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,but you've been summoned \Nto the castle this afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.75,0:04:06.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, I know. For questioning, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.96,0:04:09.44,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,May I ask you to accompany me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.44,0:04:11.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,There are things I'd like to bring back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.88,0:04:13.76,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.08,0:04:23.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, where is Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.03,0:04:25.90,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She flew off on her broom at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.90,0:04:27.36,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She made a grand show of it in secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.36,0:04:31.45,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A grand show in secret? \NWhat a strange way to describe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.45,0:04:33.28,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That is how things always are.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.38,0:04:44.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What is that noise?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.07,0:04:48.32,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The alert system that Miss Anis invented.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.32,0:04:51.05,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It sounds when someone \Nsuspicious enters the grounds
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.05,0:04:54.85,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,and sends a notification to \NMiss Anis, but this time...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.52,0:04:59.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ow...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.63,0:05:01.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I blew it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.11,0:05:05.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, good morning, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.47,0:05:07.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.16,0:05:08.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Did you have breakfast already?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.94,0:05:10.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come help me experiment, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.91,0:05:13.12,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Experiment?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.12,0:05:14.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep! Remember what I said?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.27,0:05:18.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm gonna make a special \Nmagic tool just for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.47,0:05:29.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The first thing we're \Nexperimenting with is this!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.18,0:05:33.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ta-da-da-da! A Mana Blade!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.26,0:05:36.09,Default,Euphie,0,0,0,,Here, try it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.74,0:05:41.50,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,U-Um, what am I supposed to do with...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.50,0:05:43.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just run some mana through it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.74,0:05:45.46,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,O-Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.49,0:06:04.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This is very impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.92,0:06:09.42,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Uh-huh! It's a magic sword \Nwhose blade is activated by mana!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.42,0:06:11.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The balance of spirit stones \Nis really delicate, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.61,0:06:13.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so forget about close-quarters combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.05,0:06:15.41,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's unfortunately a bit weak \Nagainst physical impact,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.35,0:06:18.13,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's extremely portable and \Neffective in magic combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.41,0:06:17.16,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but it's super strong against magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.16,0:06:19.04,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's real handy for getting rid of magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.13,0:06:21.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If it can also function as a wand, \Nit'll be quite useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.04,0:06:21.82,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Its strength and durability depend \Non how you set it up...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.51,0:06:25.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's it! Way to go, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.24,0:06:30.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Great looks, great smarts, \Nand a great personality!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.79,0:06:32.34,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,R-Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.03,0:06:37.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay, let's try this one next!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.63,0:06:55.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Are you sure this is safe? \NIt's shaking so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.60,0:06:56.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I won't die, right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.87,0:07:00.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You'll be just fine! I've got you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.27,0:07:01.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I won't let go of the back!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.28,0:07:04.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You mean that? No matter what?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.80,0:07:06.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You'd better promise!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.26,0:07:08.47,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Don't let go under any circumstances!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.47,0:07:11.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep, no matter what! I promise!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.95,0:07:13.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Royals don't lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.47,0:07:21.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm... flying?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.37,0:07:25.28,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This is what it feels like to fly?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.69,0:07:33.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, is this righ—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.91,0:07:48.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.68,0:07:54.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you okay?! I'm sorry! \NThat was an accident!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.78,0:07:56.41,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I-I mean it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.41,0:07:58.97,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I've already verified all \Nthe safety measures myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.97,0:08:00.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so I thought you'd be fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.78,0:08:05.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So, um... So, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.53,0:08:07.34,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.60,0:08:22.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Pardon my rudeness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.16,0:08:24.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No, it's totally fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.72,0:08:26.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, it really isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.91,0:08:29.07,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You are a princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.07,0:08:31.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But I'm not next in line or anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.33,0:08:32.61,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.61,0:08:36.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Besides, I am your assistant now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.59,0:08:38.33,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I must show you proper respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.33,0:08:42.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You really don't need \Nto treat this so formally.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.01,0:08:44.75,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just want you to enjoy playing right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.22,0:08:47.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Playing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.25,0:08:49.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, until you get used to it, I mean!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.51,0:08:51.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can just treat this like play!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.87,0:08:54.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And if you're gonna study, \Nyou should have fun doing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.97,0:08:58.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Devices like this have a \Nplayful element to them, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.47,0:09:01.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you're too tense with them, \Nthey'll break in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.53,0:09:09.31,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Still, we can't have you \Nplaying around {\i1}too{\i0} much.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.44,0:09:19.84,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia, it is time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.84,0:09:21.59,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Please get ready to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.59,0:09:22.28,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.81,0:09:25.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Well, Miss Anis, if you'll excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.59,0:09:26.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You have to go somewhere?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.89,0:09:28.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I've been summoned by His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.78,0:09:32.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh... Okay. See you later, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.40,0:09:52.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Has Miss Anis always been like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.72,0:09:54.85,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Most certainly not.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.85,0:09:57.06,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Long ago, she was even more reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.06,0:10:00.09,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Her absurdity, idiocy, \Nand insanity were on full display.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.72,0:10:03.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You have quite a difficult job yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.25,0:10:05.02,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I'm all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.02,0:10:07.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It's a maid's job to be at \Nthe mercy of her mistress.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.19,0:10:10.71,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,No... it's a perk, in fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.96,0:10:13.48,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A perk? Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.48,0:10:15.43,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Yes, a perk.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.23,0:10:19.13,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I guess this is all still a bit beyond me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.13,0:10:20.40,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.40,0:10:24.21,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If you don't like it, it will be best \Nfor you both if you simply say so.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.21,0:10:26.73,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh, no, it's not that I don't like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.73,0:10:27.92,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,How unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.92,0:10:32.72,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I had no idea there was anyone commendable \Nenough to find that princess favorable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.72,0:10:35.36,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Well, I wouldn't say I find her favorable...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.45,0:10:39.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The truth is that I simply don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.78,0:10:44.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I do believe she's a good person, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.46,0:10:51.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,She's just... so far from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.84,0:11:01.30,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,For crying out loud... I don't even \Nwant to look at this testimony.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.30,0:11:04.16,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I was present during the questioning,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.16,0:11:06.64,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,and he only said the same \Nthing over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.64,0:11:08.32,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.32,0:11:12.99,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I ordered Algard to remain in his chambers, \Nbut I suppose nothing has changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.45,0:11:16.11,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,He insists on choosing his own path,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.11,0:11:20.13,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,meaning he will not be bound to an \Nengagement his father chose for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.06,0:11:23.93,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,For some random person on \Nthe street, that's fine,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.93,0:11:26.16,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,but we are a royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.16,0:11:28.81,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,We have certain responsibilities!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.81,0:11:30.77,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It's not just Prince Algard.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.77,0:11:33.01,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,The other boys said very similar things.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.01,0:11:37.11,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You could try to put more pressure \Non them, but it would be difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.11,0:11:39.40,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,They're all the sons of \Nvery powerful people.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.40,0:11:41.49,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You can expect unwanted interference.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.49,0:11:48.45,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Yes... and Count Chartreuse, the Secretary \Nof Magic, is of particular concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.45,0:11:51.27,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'm sure he wants to protect his son, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.27,0:11:53.60,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,The count is a conservative leader.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.60,0:11:57.54,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Since I am supported by the reformists, \Nhe sees me as an enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.54,0:11:59.02,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,so he strongly resists me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.02,0:12:01.54,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Facing off with a conservative, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.54,0:12:03.32,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It all makes my stomach hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.52,0:12:06.48,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.66,0:12:16.84,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.38,0:12:22.04,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,So you had very little interaction \Nwith the daughter of Baron Cyan?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.04,0:12:23.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.08,0:12:26.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I once offered her some advice, \Nbut no more than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.24,0:12:28.38,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.10,0:12:34.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can't see any problem with your \Nbehavior as a betrothed noble lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.59,0:12:38.05,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Any noble should understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.05,0:12:41.10,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It doesn't sit right with me to conclude \Nthat the prince and lady overreacted
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.10,0:12:43.54,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,simply because they were maddened by love.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.54,0:12:47.19,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Do you have any other ideas \Nor realizations to share?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.19,0:12:49.90,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Though I'm sure you aren't keen \Nto recall that moment...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.54,0:12:59.21,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Everyone seemed firmly convinced \Nof their own righteousness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.47,0:13:01.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Even when he insulted me, \NI felt he was doing it
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.80,0:13:05.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,not out of malice, but simply \Nto follow his own conviction.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.35,0:13:10.33,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Those who are intoxicated by \Ntheir own sense of righteousness
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.33,0:13:13.20,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,do tend to become blind to what \Nhappens around them...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.03,0:13:18.22,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but would you mind \Ngiving me some time?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.66,0:13:21.56,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,If I come across anything, I'll contact you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.56,0:13:23.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Of course. In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.65,0:13:37.84,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.84,0:13:39.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The key to the forbidden library.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.86,0:13:42.88,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was borrowing it for \Nlessons on being a queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.41,0:13:45.11,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.11,0:13:48.46,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,If you want, you're welcome \Nto hold on to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.67,0:13:53.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I no longer have the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.49,0:13:54.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I return it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.94,0:13:58.19,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You were going through all that for us...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.47,0:14:00.45,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.45,0:14:03.15,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,N-No, Your Majesty! Please don't say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.59,0:14:04.86,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.92,0:14:11.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The prince's heart simply had no room \Nfor me in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.49,0:14:17.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But I am not deeply wounded by that fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.06,0:14:21.98,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's as if I feel nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.98,0:14:25.63,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Like everything has completely dried up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.51,0:14:30.22,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You have more than fulfilled your role.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.64,0:14:32.99,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You need not think about what comes next.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.99,0:14:36.02,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,There is nothing more you need to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.70,0:14:44.81,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Then I'll say hello to everyone here \Nwho was kind to me, and return home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.98,0:14:52.50,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Don't you think you could have \Nphrased that differently?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.50,0:14:54.46,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You never say quite enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.39,0:14:56.67,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Don't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.01,0:14:59.79,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Being a father is difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.23,0:15:01.87,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You can say that again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.90,0:15:30.51,Default,Maid,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.48,0:15:36.32,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Are you all well?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.54,0:15:40.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You all did so much for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.30,0:15:44.84,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.22,0:15:50.81,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,Had I known you were coming, \NI would have come to collect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.81,0:15:53.10,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to take up your time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.10,0:15:55.28,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I wanted to say hello to everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.28,0:15:57.05,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,You honor us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.68,0:16:00.28,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,Have you lost some weight?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.28,0:16:02.87,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, just a bit. I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.87,0:16:05.52,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,No, no. You have nothing to apologize for.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.29,0:16:08.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.31,0:16:11.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,My dress fittings will \Nno longer be necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.99,0:16:17.59,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,Your body shape never changed \Na bit, Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.59,0:16:18.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.79,0:16:20.15,Default,Grand Chamberlain,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.15,0:16:21.62,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That sounds wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.08,0:16:25.22,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The princess eats and drinks too much,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.22,0:16:28.54,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,and she always runs amok in her dresses, \Nso I have to mend them over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.54,0:16:32.60,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,And she hates corsets and bustiers. \NShe is truly a free spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.80,0:16:36.66,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can picture that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.12,0:16:43.10,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Perhaps you are just as \Nfree now, Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.10,0:16:45.79,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You don't need to wear \Ndresses or corsets anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.79,0:16:49.65,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,There is nothing to tie you down any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.85,0:16:53.32,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.02,0:17:01.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Nothing... Nothing at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.01,0:17:20.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.72,0:17:23.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis? What are you wearing?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.43,0:17:26.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry! I only slept \Nfor about two hours...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.99,0:17:28.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Actually, more like one hour...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.77,0:17:30.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, I only slept for an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.93,0:17:32.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,In fact, it's more like \NI didn't sleep at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.08,0:17:37.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry I kept you waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.10,0:17:42.46,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.46,0:17:47.23,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes! The blade is an alloy containing spirit \Nstones, making it a conductor for mana!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.87,0:17:51.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But we should probably test out \Nits mana conductivity first.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.02,0:17:53.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If it works, we can add different \Nattributes to the blade!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.84,0:17:57.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Then it'll be a luxury item \Nthat'll help you with using magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.69,0:17:59.75,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,In other words...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.75,0:18:02.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I finished your special magic tool!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.49,0:18:06.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,My own... special magic tool?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.43,0:18:08.34,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah! Now let's—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.34,0:18:11.89,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Princess, please change your clothes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.86,0:18:20.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay! Go on and try it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.98,0:18:24.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can just use that tree as a target.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.29,0:18:26.74,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What? A-Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.74,0:18:27.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Uh-huh!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.29,0:18:38.76,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Amazing... It's as though \Nit's already a part of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.24,0:18:42.74,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Fireball!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.69,0:18:53.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wow, that was awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.86,0:18:55.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well? Well? What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.15,0:18:59.33,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's an incredible item.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.74,0:19:01.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm so glad to hear it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.62,0:19:04.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay, now test it out as a magic sword, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.11,0:19:08.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Blade, assume form...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.50,0:19:12.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Water Blade!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.22,0:19:16.57,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wow! It really is a sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.39,0:19:20.89,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This is... How shall I put it? \NVery interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.37,0:19:32.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's still true.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.49,0:19:38.70,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie's magic is so beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.97,0:19:48.70,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.70,0:19:49.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Don't mention it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.88,0:19:54.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It was really fun thinking about \Nwhat would suit you best.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.84,0:19:57.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Does it... really suit me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.97,0:20:00.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sure it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.31,0:20:06.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It all started with the concept \Nof something made just for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.27,0:20:08.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It has to suit you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.81,0:20:15.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I thought of a name for it, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.06,0:20:17.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A name?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.94,0:20:18.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.09,0:20:21.70,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Arc-en-Ciel.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.95,0:20:26.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Arc... en Ciel?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.87,0:20:29.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It means "rainbow."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.26,0:20:32.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It has lots of different magic attributes,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.68,0:20:34.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and lots of colors.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.61,0:20:36.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's perfect for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.84,0:20:39.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Rainbow colors... are perfect for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.17,0:20:48.73,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you. It's a lovely name.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.42,0:20:55.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Really? I'm glad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.11,0:21:06.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.42,0:21:10.65,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It really is a perfect match.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.16,0:21:14.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I've always thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.75,0:21:18.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that you were as pretty as a rainbow.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.80,0:21:23.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You really are... so pretty, it's unfair...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.43,0:21:29.21,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.77,0:21:38.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What am I going to do with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.57,0:21:45.41,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No one has ever rested \Ntheir head on my lap before.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.56,0:21:55.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I envy you, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.44,0:22:03.37,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If I could be even the least \Nlittle bit like you...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.46,0:22:04.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Three\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Rainbow Magic Sword \Nof Longing and Reminiscence
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.97,0:23:39.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Four \N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Princess and the Lost Child\N Announce Their Decision
